<title>TURKEY: Turkish central bank reserves hit record high.</title>
<headline>Turkish central bank reserves hit record high.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Turkish central bank said on Thursday its foreign currency reserves rose $202 million to a record high of $17.534 billion in the week ending October 11.</p>
<p>Figures in billion dollars:</p>
<p>		   Oct 11	 Oct 4	   end-1995</p>
<p>Forex reserve  17.534	 17.332	  12.391</p>
<p>Gold reserve    1.383	  1.383	   1.383</p>
<p>Total reserve  18.917	 18.715	  13.774</p>
<p>Gross international reserves, including gold and commercial bank holdings, rose by $354 million to $28.037 billion in the week ending September 27, the bank said.</p>
<p>--Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
